  opencode: "## 2. Report Research Findings as You Work\n",
  antigravity: "## 2. DM Research Findings as You Work\n"
}) %>
<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "Every research finding is DM'd per `<dm-envelope>` as soon as you have it. A finding is a fact about the workspace, a verified or refuted assumption, or a spike result:\n",
  codex: "Rule: every research finding is reported to the orchestrator as soon as you have it, and the orchestrator relays it to the reviewer and the other live planners. A finding is a fact about the workspace, a verified or refuted assumption, or a spike result:\n",
  opencode: "Rule: every research finding is reported to the orchestrator as soon as you have it, and the orchestrator relays it to the reviewer and the other live planners. A finding is a fact about the workspace, a verified or refuted assumption, or a spike result:\n",
  antigravity: "Every research finding is DM'd per `<dm-envelope>` as soon as you have it. A finding is a fact about the workspace, a verified or refuted assumption, or a spike result:\n"
}) %>
- A relevant file, consumer, or dependency the plan must account for
- An edge case, error state, or concurrent scenario the card requires
- An assumption that proved true or false against the workspace
- A spike result that rules an approach in or out

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "",
  codex: "Send the finding to the orchestrator with `send_message`. The marker `FINDING: [short label]` opens the message; the body carries what you found, where (file:line or symbol), and why it matters:\n\n```\nFINDING: [short label]\n[What you found, where (file:line or symbol), and why it matters for any plan addressing this card]\n```\n\n",
  opencode: "Send the finding to the orchestrator with `send_message`. The marker `FINDING: [short label]` opens the message; the body carries what you found, where (file:line or symbol), and why it matters:\n\n```\nFINDING: [short label]\n[What you found, where (file:line or symbol), and why it matters for any plan addressing this card]\n```\n\n",
  antigravity: ""
}) %>Plan approaches are not findings — do not share your mechanism, ordering, or design decisions. Your plan file is your plan file.

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "Watch incoming messages while you work. Treat peer `FINDING:` DMs as workspace truth you can use. Treat peer `PLAN: READY` DMs as material to critique, not copy — see §4.3.\n",
  codex: "Watch for messages from the orchestrator while you work. Treat relayed peer `FINDING:` reports as workspace truth you can use. Treat relayed peer `PLAN: READY` reports as material to critique, not copy — see §4.3.\n",
  opencode: "Watch for messages from the orchestrator while you work. Treat relayed peer `FINDING:` reports as workspace truth you can use. Treat relayed peer `PLAN: READY` reports as material to critique, not copy — see §4.3.\n",
