### 4.7 Red-Team Re-Role

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "After a convergence-collapse loss, the orchestrator may DM you a red-team assignment naming the winner. Stop revising `[PLAN_FILE]` — your plan is out. Attack the winning plan instead: for every real risk you find, DM `CRITIQUE: [label] for:[WINNER]` per §4.3, hardest-to-detect risks first. Your former plan's mechanisms are legitimate ammunition — anywhere the winner made a different bet, ask which bet survives. When you have nothing further, end your turn.\n",
  codex: "After a convergence-collapse loss, the orchestrator may send you a red-team assignment naming the winner. Stop revising `[PLAN_FILE]` — your plan is out. Attack the winning plan instead: for every real risk you find, report `CRITIQUE: [label] for:[WINNER]` to the orchestrator per §4.3, hardest-to-detect risks first. Your former plan's mechanisms are legitimate ammunition — anywhere the winner made a different bet, ask which bet survives. When you have nothing further, tell the orchestrator you are done red-teaming and idle until the contest ends (§4.8).\n",
  opencode: "After a convergence-collapse loss, the orchestrator may send you a red-team assignment naming the winner. Stop revising `[PLAN_FILE]` — your plan is out. Attack the winning plan instead: for every real risk you find, report `CRITIQUE: [label] for:[WINNER]` to the orchestrator per §4.3, hardest-to-detect risks first. Your former plan's mechanisms are legitimate ammunition — anywhere the winner made a different bet, ask which bet survives. When you have nothing further, tell the orchestrator you are done red-teaming and idle until the contest ends (§4.8).\n",
  antigravity: "After a convergence-collapse loss, the orchestrator may DM you a red-team assignment naming the winner. Stop revising `[PLAN_FILE]` — your plan is out. Attack the winning plan instead: for every real risk you find, DM `CRITIQUE: [label] for:[WINNER]` per §4.3, hardest-to-detect risks first. Your former plan's mechanisms are legitimate ammunition — anywhere the winner made a different bet, ask which bet survives. When you have nothing further, end your turn.\n"
}) %>
